   "proposition":"The English says the '+' printed by a Surv object marks an observation that was right-censored; the Turkish says it marks whether an observation was 'doğru sansürlenip', that is correctly censored.",
   "reader_consequence":"A Turkish reader reading the printed survobj output takes '+' to mean the censoring was done correctly, rather than that the follow-up time is a lower bound because the event was not observed.",
